.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt AFPLAY 1
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm afplay
.Nd play a sound file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v Ar volume
.Op Fl t Ar time
.Op Fl r Ar rate
.Op Fl q Ar quality
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl h
.Ar audio_file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
plays
.Ar audio_file
on the default output device, in any format AudioToolbox reads (WAVE,
AIFF, AIFC and CAF of linear PCM), and returns when it has played.
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl v Ar volume
The playback volume: 1 is the file's own level, 0 is silence and values
above 1 amplify.
.It Fl t Ar time
Play only the first
.Ar time
seconds.
.It Fl r Ar rate
The playback rate; only 1 for now.
.It Fl q Ar quality
The quality of the rate conversion to the device: 0 for low, 1 for high
(the default).
.It Fl d
Show the file's type, format and length before playing it.
.It Fl h
Show a short help.
.El
.Pp
An interrupt stops the playback at once.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 once the file has played, 130 when interrupted, 1 on an error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr open 1
